190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Employability and skills mismatch refers to the gap between the skills employers seek and those possessed by job seekers, exacerbated by rapid technological advancements, outdated educational curricula, and evolving job requirements. This misalignment particularly affects graduates and employers. A management plan aims to bridge this gap by aligning education with industry needs, promoting lifelong learning, and utilizing data-driven solutions for real-time labor market tracking and skills matching. Collaboration among educational institutions, employers, policymakers, and individuals is essential to address this issue.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The executive summary addresses the pressing issue of employability and skills mismatch, where there is a significant gap between the skills employers seek and those possessed by job seekers. This misalignment is intensified by rapid technological changes, outdated educational curricula, and evolving job requirements, leading to challenges for both graduates and employers. Consequently, this issue contributes to high youth unemployment rates and difficulty in filling positions with suitably skilled candidates.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To bridge this gap, a comprehensive management plan is proposed, emphasizing the alignment of education with industry needs and the promotion of lifelong learning. The plan leverages data-driven solutions for real-time labor market tracking and skills matching to ensure educational programs are relevant and up-to-date. Collaboration among educational institutions, employers, policymakers, and individuals is essential for creating a dynamic and responsive labor market. The empathy map technique is employed to understand the experiences, thoughts, and feelings of job seekers, providing insights that help tailor effective solutions.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, the Lotus Blossom technique is recommended for brainstorming and developing innovative solutions to address the skills mismatch. This method systematically explores core issues and their related aspects, leading to comprehensive strategies. By incorporating these approaches, the management plan aims to equip graduates with the necessary skills demanded by employers, enhancing employability. Ultimately, addressing the employability and skills mismatch will improve labor market efficiency, boost economic productivity, and promote social inclusion, benefiting individuals, businesses, and society as a whole.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
