210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The persistently high youth unemployment rates in regions like the Middle East and parts of Europe suggest significant issues with employability and skills mismatch. Despite stable unemployment figures from 2014 to 2015, many young people struggle to find jobs that match their qualifications and skills. This indicates a need for better alignment between educational systems and labour market demands, as well as more effective vocational training programs to bridge the gap between the skills young people possess and the needs of employers.)
/E (The persistently high youth unemployment rates in regions like the Middle East and parts of Europe suggest significant issues with employability and skills mismatch. Despite stable unemployment figures from 2014 to 2015, many young people struggle to find jobs that match their qualifications and skills. This indicates a need for better alignment between educational systems and labour market demands, as well as more effective vocational training programs to bridge the gap between the skills young people possess and the needs of employers.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The primary objective of this management plan is to bridge the gap between employability and skills mismatch. This objective is pivotal as it directly addresses the core issue at the heart of unemployment and underemployment: the misalignment between the skills possessed by job seekers and those demanded by employers. By focusing on bridging this gap, the management plan seeks to enhance the efficiency of the labour market, improve economic productivity, and promote social inclusion. Furthermore, by supporting lifelong learning and aligning education with industry needs, the plan lays the groundwork for sustainable solutions that empower individuals and drive economic growth. Ultimately, by making bridging the gap between employability and skills mismatch the central focus, the management plan endeavours to create more resilient, inclusive, and dynamic labour markets that benefit individuals, businesses, and society as a whole.)
/E (The primary objective of this management plan is to bridge the gap between employability and skills mismatch. This objective is pivotal as it directly addresses the core issue at the heart of unemployment and underemployment: the misalignment between the skills possessed by job seekers and those demanded by employers. By focusing on bridging this gap, the management plan seeks to enhance the efficiency of the labour market, improve economic productivity, and promote social inclusion. Furthermore, by supporting lifelong learning and aligning education with industry needs, the plan lays the groundwork for sustainable solutions that empower individuals and drive economic growth. Ultimately, by making bridging the gap between employability and skills mismatch the central focus, the management plan endeavours to create more resilient, inclusive, and dynamic labour markets that benefit individuals, businesses, and society as a whole.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
