222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Problem Statement: Many job seekers struggle to find employment due to a mismatch between their current skills and the skills demanded by employers in the evolving job market. Due to a lack of experience and practical abilities, recent graduates are finding it difficult to get employment in their professions of choice, which causes them to become frustrated and anxious about their future careers. Their professional development is hampered by this mismatch in skills, which also affects the productivity and creative potential of companies that struggle to fill positions with qualified workers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In an economy that demands more skill sets and sophisticated technical knowledge, graduates are seen as potential essential participants in the push to improve value-added products and services. However, the place of graduates in the economy is still debatable and subject to differing opinions. Their reputation as holders of an exclusive and well-preserved core of technical, professional, and managerial jobs has been called into question by structural transformations in both higher education and the economy. They were once described as a "social elite" \(Kelsall et al., 1972\). )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
