266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The skills mismatch often leads to high rates of unemployment and underemployment. Job seekers may find it difficult to secure positions that match their qualifications, leading to financial instability and potential long-term career stagnation. Skill mismatches contribute significantly to youth unemployment rates, as many young people are entering the workforce with skills that do not align with current market demands.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <B72044656372656173656420436F6E666964656E636520616E64206D6F7469766174696F6E3A>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Continuous job rejections can erode self-esteem and motivation. The psychological impact of prolonged job searching, and perceived inadequacy can lead to decreased job search intensity and longer periods of unemployment. A study by McKinsey & Company found that job seekers facing skill mismatches often experience frustration and a sense of hopelessness, which can negatively affect their mental health and overall well-being.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <B720536B696C6C204F62736F6C657363656E63653A>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Skills can become obsolete in several ways: through aging, which reduces certain manual abilities \(physical obsolescence\); through technological or economic changes that render specific skills unnecessary \(economic obsolescence\); and through lack of use, leading to their underutilization \(Van Loo et al., 2001\). Without opportunities to apply and update their skills, job seekers' abilities can become obsolete. This issue is exacerbated by rapid technological advancements, which continually shift the skill requirements across various industries. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
