280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To bridge the skill gap, employers often need to invest in additional training for new hires. This increases operational costs and can strain resources, particularly for small and medium-sized enterprises \(SMEs\). The need for ongoing training to keep up with rapid technological advancements adds a recurring expense, further impacting their financial stability. As a result, some SMEs may experience reduced profitability and slower growth due to the continuous investment required to ensure their workforce is adequately skilled.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 152 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (FOR THE ECONOMY)
/E (FOR THE ECONOMY)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <B720526564756365642050726F6475637469766974793A20>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A workforce that is not fully utilized or appropriately skilled can lead to lower overall productivity. The mismatch results in inefficiencies as employees may not perform optimally in roles for which they are not adequately trained. This can cause delays in project completion, reduced quality of work, and higher error rates. When employees struggle to meet job demands due to inadequate skills, it can also lead to increased supervision and management intervention, diverting resources from other critical business functions. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <B720536F6369616C20496E657175616C6974793A20>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A lack of connectivity between individuals and employment prospects is sometimes referred to as poor job accessibility \(Kain, 1992\). Skills mismatches can exacerbate income inequality and limit social mobility. Individuals from disadvantaged backgrounds may have less access to quality education and training opportunities, widening the gap between different socio-economic groups. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
