<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 661 0 R
/ActualText (Personal Development Plans - When companies help employees plan their careers and keep learning new skills, everyone wins. Employees stay motivated and feel valued, and the company benefits from having skilled and engaged workers who are less likely to leave.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 662 0 R
/ActualText (Educational Reforms - Updating school curriculums to include practical skills, digital know-how, and teamwork better prepares students for the real world. This makes it easier for them to get jobs and helps employers find people who are ready for the future market.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 663 0 R
/ActualText (Skills Assessments - Before hiring someone, it's good to know if they actually have the skills they say they do. Skills assessments give idea what someone can do, so we can focus on the people who are a great fit for the job and save time and cost.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 664 0 R
/ActualText (Gender-Specific Support: Provide support, especially for young females who disproportionately suffer from unemployment. Gender-specific programs can help bridge the gender gap in the labor market, contributing to greater inclusivity and equality and attract skilled talent.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
