356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 665 0 R
/ActualText (Inclusive Communication Channels - We'll ensure everyone  we reach out to everyone in ways they're comfortable with. Whether it's through emails, social media, or face-to-face meetings, we want everyone to feel welcoming and involved. There are two types of communication - Internal and external.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 666 0 R
/ActualText (  Engage Everyone: Let's start by getting everyone involved in the conversation. Regular talks with graduates, employers, educators, government folks, and industry representatives will help us stay in sync and address any issues as they come up.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 667 0 R
/ActualText (Mix It Up: People like to hear things in different ways. We'll use emails, newsletters, social media, and webinars to make sure everyone gets the message, no matter how they like to communicate.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 668 0 R
/ActualText (Speak Their Language: We'll make sure our messages hit home by tailoring them to what each group cares about most. For graduates, that might mean stories of success and encouragement. For educators and employers, it might be data on the impact of our programs.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
