370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The TechSkills initiative by TechCorp demonstrates how a multi-faceted approach to addressing skills mismatch can yield significant benefits for all stakeholders involved. By leveraging data-driven solutions, addressing socio-economic issues, and meeting stakeholder needs, TechCorp successfully improved their recruitment processes, employee satisfaction, and overall workforce quality. This case study serves as a robust example of how companies can strategically tackle skills mismatch and create a more efficient, inclusive, and dynamic work environment. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In essence, there are some major findings: first, a poor match between available and required skills strongly affects job satisfaction negatively, and second, female workers are particularly disadvantaged by nepotism and the overall labour market practices. Despite their educational level, their participation in the labour market remains limited and their wages are lower than their male counterparts. Through collective effort and steadfast commitment, we can transform the challenge of employability and skills mismatch into an avenue for empowerment, progress, and prosperity for all. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
